{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dem terrain displacement for vfx dem terrain displacement for vfx","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX.md","fileName":"DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Matte Painting and Scene Finishing]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matte Painting and Scene Finishing","Manual Perspective-Plane Scene Extraction","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dem terrain displacement for vfx dem terrain displacement for vfx","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX.md","fileName":"DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX","heading":"DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A digital elevation model stores sampled elevation in a grid whose values can drive displacement of a subdivided plane. A dark-looking DEM may hold useful values in a narrow range, so levels can reveal its heights before it is applied. Subdivision must be increased cautiously: too little looks jagged, while excessive detail burdens the machine. The book notes that radar-derived elevation may represent the first reflected surface, including treetops or buildings, rather than bare ground. A matching aerial image can texture the resulting terrain. See [[Manual Perspective-Plane Scene Extraction]] for another source-image-to-scene method.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matte Painting and Scene Finishing","Manual Perspective-Plane Scene Extraction","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dem terrain displacement for vfx dem terrain displacement for vfx","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX.md","fileName":"DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"DEM Terrain Displacement for VFX","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matte Painting and Scene Finishing","Manual Perspective-Plane Scene Extraction","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}